{
  "id": "Compound::DB00671 - Gene::6565",
  "verbalization": "Cefixime, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is shown to bind to Slc15a1, a protein involved in transport activities across cellular membranes. This binding is linked to the participation of Slc15a1 in various transport processes, including proton-dependent peptide transport and proton/oligonucleotide cotransport. These mechanisms suggest that Slc15a1 functions as a transporter that facilitates the movement of specific molecules across the cell membrane, often in a coupled manner with protons. The evidence indicates that Cefixime may interact with Slc15a1 through its binding site, potentially modulating its transport activity. The shared participation of Slc15a2 in these transport processes implies a functional relationship between Slc15a1 and Slc15a2, possibly through a common regulatory or structural role in membrane transport. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc15a1 as a central player in the transport of peptides and nucleotides, with Cefixime potentially influencing this process by interacting with Slc15a1.",
